  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"112\" data-end=\"357\"><strong data-start=\"112\" data-end=\"124\">Chloride</strong> is a key extracellular electrolyte involved in maintaining <strong data-start=\"184\" data-end=\"204\">osmotic pressure</strong>, <strong data-start=\"206\" data-end=\"223\">fluid balance</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"229\" data-end=\"254\">acid-base equilibrium</strong>. Measuring chloride in <strong data-start=\"278\" data-end=\"293\">body fluids</strong> (such as pleural, peritoneal, or cerebrospinal fluid) helps in:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"359\" data-end=\"569\">\n<li data-start=\"359\" data-end=\"419\">\n<p data-start=\"361\" data-end=\"419\"><strong data-start=\"361\" data-end=\"406\">Differentiating transudates from exudates</strong> in effusions</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"420\" data-end=\"505\">\n<p data-start=\"422\" data-end=\"505\">Evaluating <strong data-start=\"433\" data-end=\"462\">fluid composition changes</strong> due to infections, inflammation, or trauma</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"506\" data-end=\"569\">\n<p data-start=\"508\" data-end=\"569\">Assessing <strong data-start=\"518\" data-end=\"544\">acid-base disturbances</strong> within body compartments</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"628\" data-end=\"689\">Increased chloride concentration in body fluids may indicate:</p>\n<div class=\"_tableContainer_80l1q_1\">\n<div class=\"_tableWrapper_80l1q_14 group flex w-fit flex-col-reverse\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"691\" data-end=\"1296\">\n<thead data-start=\"691\" data-end=\"798\">\n<tr data-start=\"691\" data-end=\"798\">\n<th data-start=\"691\" data-end=\"727\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"693\" data-end=\"713\">Clinical Context</strong></th>\n<th data-start=\"727\" data-end=\"798\" data-col-size=\"lg\"><strong data-start=\"729\" data-end=\"747\">Possible Cause</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody data-start=\"907\" data-end=\"1296\">\n<tr data-start=\"907\" data-end=\"1023\">\n<td data-start=\"907\" data-end=\"943\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"909\" data-end=\"938\">Cerebrospinal fluid (CSF)</strong></td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"943\" data-end=\"1023\">Seen in <strong data-start=\"953\" data-end=\"968\">dehydration</strong>, <strong data-start=\"970\" data-end=\"988\">hyperchloremia</strong>, or systemic metabolic disorders</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"1024\" data-end=\"1174\">\n<td data-start=\"1024\" data-end=\"1063\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"1026\" data-end=\"1062\">Pleural/peritoneal/ascitic fluid</strong></td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"1063\" data-end=\"1174\">May suggest <strong data-start=\"1077\" data-end=\"1098\">serous transudate</strong> due to systemic illness (e.g., congestive heart failure, liver cirrhosis)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"1175\" data-end=\"1296\">\n<td data-start=\"1175\" data-end=\"1217\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"1177\" data-end=\"1216\">Exogenous infusion or contamination</strong></td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"1217\" data-end=\"1296\">Bicarbonate-chloride exchange (e.g., with saline infusions) or lab artifact</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
